 ## Alpha 8 - Semantic-preserving optimisation remodel
 
-Alpha8 changes the optimisation rule from "try hard, then fall back" to "never cross the semantic boundary in the first place".
+Alpha8 changes the optimisation rule to "never cross the semantic boundary in the first place".
 
 Implemented surfaces:
 
 - `AGCSemanticInvariant`: runtime ledger for read-only preparation, ordered commits, deadline batches and conflict-serialised waves.
 - `AGCDeterministicTaskPipeline`: worker-side immutable preparation followed by primary-thread sequence-ordered commits.
 - `AGCWorldConcurrencyPlanner`: builds a per-tick world conflict plan. Full parallel world waves are allowed only when plugin and runtime signals prove that Bukkit-visible callbacks and world mutations remain deterministic. Otherwise worlds keep ordered commits while AGC can still do safe planning/accounting.
-- Network admission now records deadline-preserved batching instead of treating immediate flush as an emergency fallback.
+- Network admission records deadline-preserved batching and immediate-order preservation as first-class decisions.
 - Chunk admission now records ordered queue commits and fair-token waits; queued chunks are still never dropped or reordered.
 - Runtime health now drains deterministic commits and prefers semantic budget tightening over disabling packet/chunk optimisations.
 - `/agc semantics` mirrors `/agc safety` and shows the semantic invariant ledger, planner and deterministic task pipeline state.
 
 The production goal remains unchanged: aggressive defaults are allowed only where the algorithm itself preserves Minecraft feel, Bukkit callback order, chunk ordering, redstone/factory timing and packet deadlines.
+
+
+## Alpha 9 - No-invasion optimisation remodel
+
+Alpha9 implements the requested change to “do not invade gameplay semantics in the first place.” The new rule is that every optimisation must enter through a lane that already preserves vanilla/Paper-visible behaviour:
+
+- `AGCNoInvasionOptimizer` is the central lane arbiter. It records `IMMEDIATE_ORDERED`, `DEADLINE_ORDERED_BATCH`, `FIFO_FAIR_WAIT`, `READ_ONLY_PREPARE`, `CONFLICT_FREE_WAVE`, and `ORDERED_COMMIT` decisions.
+- Network optimisation uses deadline-ordered batching only for non-interactive packets and only within the configured one-tick deadline. Interactive packets remain immediate.
+- Chunk optimisation uses `AGCChunkFairQueue`, a per-player FIFO deficit queue. It never drops queued chunks and never reorders a player’s queue head.
+- Entity optimisation uses `AGCEntitySnapshotPlanner` for read-only tracker preparation. It does not skip entity ticks, damage, interaction, AI, or Bukkit events.
+- Multi-world optimisation uses `AGCWorldWriteIntentGraph`; risky plugin/cross-world signals add conflict edges, so only edge-free world groups run together. Commit waves keep deterministic order.
+- The parallel world tick loop now executes planner waves instead of blindly dispatching every world at once.
+- Added `/agc noinvasion` and R17 reflection tests.
+
+Aggressive defaults remain enabled, but the alpha9 implementation treats compatibility as an invariant of the algorithm, not a post-failure switch.
