+### AGC 26.2 alpha9 no-invasion remodel
+
+Alpha9 pushes the rule further: AGC should not depend on trying unsafe work first. Optimisations now declare a no-invasion lane before they run:
+
+- `AGCNoInvasionOptimizer` coordinates all aggressive paths as deadline-ordered batching, FIFO fair queueing, read-only snapshot planning, conflict-free world waves, or ordered commits.
+- `AGCChunkFairQueue` preserves each player’s chunk FIFO order while using deficit tokens to stop one player or arena from monopolising load/generate starts.
+- `AGCEntitySnapshotPlanner` only admits read-only entity tracker preparation; entity ticks, damage, interaction and plugin events are never skipped.
+- `AGCWorldWriteIntentGraph` builds per-tick conflict waves. Worlds in the same wave have no write-intent edge; waves commit sequentially, so cross-world/plugin-visible work stays deterministic.
+- `MinecraftServer.meteus$tickLevelsParallel(...)` now consumes planner waves instead of blindly running every world together.
+
+Use `/agc noinvasion` to inspect the no-invasion lanes, FIFO chunk queue, entity snapshot planner and write-intent graph.
